  "composer": {
    "rawText": "[SongTitle: Bronce y Azúcar]\r\n[Style: latin, big band, Afro-Cuban jazz, clean studio recording, expressive male vocal]\r\n[Caption: Brass, rhythm, and heat in a Havana night.]\r\n[Image: Vintage Havana bar, brass section glowing under warm lights.]\r\n[Refresh Title: Cuba Libre]\r\n[Theme: Drinks]\r\n[Gradients: 6]\r\n[Rank: 6]\r\n[TitleRarityPct: 0.75]\r\n[Seeds: 596, A:89, B:85, C:81, D:75]\r\n[Created: January 27, 2026 at 9:28 PM]\r\n[Composer Version: v2.0]\r\n\r\n[Plan]\r\n[Perspective: we_community]\r\n[Concept: celebration, resilience, and shared rhythm over a classic drink]\r\n[Topic: Night & Social Energy → dance_floor_release]\r\n[GenreBias: latin → big band Cuban]\r\n[StyleChange: none]\r\n[Modulation: none]\r\n[HookProminence: high]\r\n[Deviation: brass-driven swing]\r\n\r\n[Intro]\r\n[Full brass fanfare, congas and timbales answer, walking bass locks in.]\r\nLa noche cae sobre el ron  \r\nBronce vibra en el salón  \r\n\r\n[Verse]\r\n[Syncopated melody, call-and-response with trumpets.]\r\nHielo canta en vaso corto  \r\nLima corta el calor roto  \r\nViejas risas, mesa fiel  \r\nSudor brilla en la pared  \r\n\r\n[Verse]\r\n[Trombones slide wide, rhythm section pushes forward.]\r\nManos juntas al compás  \r\nCada pena baila atrás  \r\nNo hay reloj que mande aquí  \r\nSolo el pulso y el maní  \r\n\r\n[Chorus]\r\n[Big band hits, stacked vocals, joyful release.]\r\nCuba Libre, fuego y son  \r\nAzúcar, ron y corazón  \r\nCuando el mundo pesa más  \r\nEste ritmo nos da paz  \r\n\r\n[Verse]\r\n[Lower register, swaggering phrasing.]\r\nCalles guardan lo que fue  \r\nSueños vivos otra vez  \r\nBrindis alto, voz sincera  \r\nHoy la pena no gobierna  \r\n\r\n[Bridge]\r\n[Break to percussion, then brass rebuilds in waves.]\r\nToca lento, deja arder  \r\nQue la noche sabe hacer  \r\n\r\n[Final Chorus]\r\n[Full ensemble, trumpets soar, trombones punch.]\r\nCuba Libre, fuego y son  \r\nAzúcar, ron y corazón  \r\nSi mañana quiere entrar  \r\nQue nos encuentre al bailar  \r\n\r\n[Ending]\r\n[Final brass hit, percussion flourish, crowd shout.]\r\nSalud, mi gente, hasta el sol  \r\nQue despierte este tambor  \r\n",
